{"id": "EUVD-2026-76251", "enisaUuid": "3cb323bf-d681-3b04-8eab-f4633498ee78", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmack: fix cred UAF in smack_file_send_sigiotask()\n\nWhen inspecting the credentials of another task, objective credentials\n(->real_cred, accessed with __task_cred()) must always be used.\n\nAccessing ->cred on a non-current task is forbidden unless that task is\nbeing created or destroyed; a task is allowed to change its own ->cred\npointer with no synchronization, and changing ->cred should only affect the\ncurrent syscall.\n\nsmack_file_send_sigiotask() was accessing both sets of credentials: First\ntsk->cred, then __task_cred(tsk).\n\nFix it, always access the objective credentials here.\n\nI have tested that this bug can lead to a KASAN-reported UAF of struct cred\nin smack_file_send_sigiotask(), and that this fix prevents the race.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:42:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:45:12", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a512366d84e134a9eefc2cc40eeb6e80e2ec162c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7c7fe043f3099d0d35002b248967f75e55345b93", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f9c7b1f2b9d8f4176d2632743f51400855978ace", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b5bcf3adfa27279da4401ab8f1e1a706601a92be", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ed64aa505875a3b4defd504ee8e59e1949246a62", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b791401bf389a1546a830d2b381ca60fe94c7870", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fedc88e38ce979a720cd2de042578cb5df3dc8de"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80928", "GHSA-pw4j-jrv7-fq3m"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0881d592-e806-3512-b7eb-d2dd1b4a4f8f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "115ef936-7e58-37f4-b0e5-f7845db75e7c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "1f019c2c-86fc-32bb-897a-3a1c29615c16", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "20ffc050-7905-3285-ac6d-6f4cd5103c8d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b11a1decef07c19443d24ae926982bc8ec9f4c0 <ed64aa505875a3b4defd504ee8e59e1949246a62"}, {"id": "2a9e449e-1b75-3c10-933b-b0571550da45", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "4cb98a8b-7343-3b04-9d4c-1b2f63156ef1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.29"}, {"id": "6d5d6b5e-5c8d-382d-8f67-765efdd4b1f1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "9cc8942a-17d7-3c3d-9d36-7b0b2cd57ec0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b11a1decef07c19443d24ae926982bc8ec9f4c0 <b791401bf389a1546a830d2b381ca60fe94c7870"}, {"id": "9e426024-f2f3-3fce-8bbd-e07b082f718f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "9fb3fc0e-8755-3f79-929e-5879b38e311b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b11a1decef07c19443d24ae926982bc8ec9f4c0 <7c7fe043f3099d0d35002b248967f75e55345b93"}, {"id": "a21aee49-caf1-3f3e-b2e0-efa2141bef2b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b11a1decef07c19443d24ae926982bc8ec9f4c0 <f9c7b1f2b9d8f4176d2632743f51400855978ace"}, {"id": "bad6260a-cdf6-3927-acfe-e9755e02a64f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b11a1decef07c19443d24ae926982bc8ec9f4c0 <a512366d84e134a9eefc2cc40eeb6e80e2ec162c"}, {"id": "d522b86c-4537-3f80-9005-b02e2fa71f3c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3b11a1decef07c19443d24ae926982bc8ec9f4c0 <b5bcf3adfa27279da4